WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.837
♪ (ROCK MUSIC FADES IN) ♪

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.472
Hello, everybody!

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:11.144
Maybe you noticed this isn't
like a regular concert.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:18.951
<i> The show is about our history
 as Americans.</i>

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:20.920
That history is in our songs.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.989
(CROWD CHEERING)

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.891
<i> I knew I wanted to do
 the whole show</i>

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.293
<i> as a 24-hour performance.</i>

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.096
<i> But I only wanted
 to do it once.</i>

00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:35.535
Today, tonight, and tomorrow.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:36.969
SPEAKER:
<i> It's a 24-hour performance</i>

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.138
<i> that asked us to practice joy</i>

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.407
and exuberance
and maximalism.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.242
I got totally inspired.

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.778
<i> It was like, "Oh, my God.
 I get to make 24 historical,</i>

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:47.380
<i> like, period costumes."</i>

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.383
TAYLOR MAC:
<i> Part of the art was that</i>

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.086
<i> the audience would be with us
 for 24 hours, as well.</i>

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:56.956
<i> ♪ War, children ♪</i>

00:00:57.456 --> 00:01:02.428
<i> ♪ It's just a shot away
 It's just a shot away ♪</i>

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:06.699
SPEAKER 2:
<i> Taylor's created something
 that is a radical format.</i>

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.402
Gloria, Gloria!

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:12.439
<i> ♪ Gloria, Gloria! ♪</i>

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:15.374
<i> ♪ Gloria, Gloria! ♪</i>

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.610
TAYLOR MAC:<i> The audience,
 they start to support us more.</i>

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.946
<i> We lose energy on stage,
 but they give more energy.</i>

00:01:21.046 --> 00:01:23.950
<i> ♪ It is decreed
 The people rule ♪</i>

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.885
<i> ♪ It is decreed
 The people rule ♪</i>

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.654
<i> I'm interested in what happens</i>

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:31.123
<i> when the audience has to make
 a commitment to something.</i>

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.126
<i> It stops being
 just a party game.</i>

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.994
It becomes something deeper.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.529
♪ (UKELELE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:40.099
The reason we have problems
is lack of community.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.570
<i> ♪ When all the artists
 Leave or die ♪</i>

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.773
<i> An artist's job is
 to dream the culture forward.</i>

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.942
<i> ♪ And you're alone ♪</i>

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:54.380
<i> To look at the things
 that aren't working in society</i>

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.082
<i> and imagine
 how it could be better.</i>

00:01:57.282 --> 00:01:58.618
<i> ♪ You can lie down ♪</i>

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.486
<i> Ultimately, for me,
 it's all about</i>

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.588
<i> experiencing the full range
 of who you are</i>

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.258
<i> and taking the time
 to actually do that.</i>

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:09.329
<i> ♪ You can lie down
 Or get up and play ♪</i>

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:16.236
(CROWD SINGS)<i> ♪ You can lie down
 Or get up and play ♪</i>

